@sathyanarays parallelism is mutable all the time, we can't restrict it (that would not be backward compatible anyways)

As Daniel mentioned, the semantics for allowing to mutate completions is if the before and after the update completions=parallelism. 

If completions != parallelism, then there is still a path to mutate completions over two updates: 1) update parallelism = completions; 2) update completions and parallelism together.
